# Skill messages use the names of the skills window (owner report 2026-10-23: "You advanced to axe fighting level 43." while the
# window shows one Melee row; server/README.md "One melee skill", "Skill names in messages"). New getSkillMessageName() in
# tools.cpp: sword, club and axe fighting are "melee", distance fighting is "ranged", every other skill keeps the engine's
# name (fist fighting, shielding, fishing, the crafting skills, magic level). Player::addSkillAdvance ("You advanced to ..."),
# Player::addSkillTries (the same line), Player::removeSkillTries ("You were downgraded to ...") and Player::setSkill*
# ("Your Melee skill changed from level ...") use it. getSkillName itself stays: the item look texts read it and
# data/scripts/chaos/melee_skill_look.lua rewrites "club fighting +2, sword fighting +2, axe fighting +2" to "melee +2".
# A server rebuild is needed. Apply in the server source root after 0001-0064: patch -p1 < 0065-skill-message-names.patch.
